From 78be12785bc1d82d7de23377c9d46e9a70f0fb07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 07:22:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www: surface the owner's guide everywhere (backlog P2)

The master guide (docs/REAPER-GUIDE.md) existed since v2.7.1 but nothing
on the router pointed at it. Now:

- shell topbar + dashboard topbar: a '?' button on every page opens the
  guide (new tab, rel=noopener; the router never fetches it)
- Firewall / Gatekeeper / Warden / Storage / USB pages: a '?' dot beside
  the page title deep-links the matching guide section (4.1/4.2/4.3/
  4.11/4.12); Policy Routing keeps its dedicated VPN-ROUTING-GUIDE dot
- first-boot page: a one-line mention under the credential form
- About page already gained its Owner's Guide button (previous commit)

Tooltips reuse RABT_43; RABT_46 is the first-boot line (25 dicts
lockstep 6762). All eight pages' JS parse clean, ASCII clean.
